# Capture artifacts are sensitive (CLAUDE.md §3.4): they may contain
# response bodies, storage state, and user content. Never commit them.
#
# Root-anchored. An unanchored `capture/` matches a directory of that name at
# ANY depth — which silently swallowed the whole `packages/capture/` source
# package: every "capture:" commit up to 819121b contained schema and docs
# changes only, and the crawler existed nowhere but a working tree.
/capture/
# The schema fixtures are a capture tree on purpose, and no longer need an
# exception now that the pattern is anchored — kept as a tripwire in case it
# is ever un-anchored again.
!/packages/schema/fixtures/capture/
**/auth/storage-state.json

# Generated environments
envs/*/
!envs/.gitkeep

# LLM call cache (CLAUDE.md §13)
.siteforge-cache/


node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
